WEBVTT

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:06.320
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning all, quick one. Tuesday 29th, let's get through stand-up. Everyone alright?</v>

00:00:07.719 --> 00:00:16.120
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, not bad. Bit grim out though, isn't it? Proper autumn now. Weekend's meant to be a washout as well, if the forecast's right.</v>

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:21.690
<v Callum Reid>You say that every week, Tom, then you're out doing barbecue in a hoodie.</v>

00:00:23.839 --> 00:00:25.940
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah well, optimistic engineering judgement, that.</v>

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:34.009
<v Aisha Begum>Speaking of important matters, there's still birthday cake in the office fridge from yesterday, if nobody's nicked it yet.</v>

00:00:35.159 --> 00:00:36.909
<v Jamie Brennan>Right, that's breakfast sorted then.</v>

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:42.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, priorities in order. Safety first, cake second. Callum, production?</v>

00:00:43.869 --> 00:00:58.920
<v Callum Reid>Line-wise, mostly okay. I did see the pressure on the Line 1 Mould Temperature Controller dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own, so just keeping an eye on it. Not asking for anything off the back of it yet.</v>

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.469
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, noted, just an observation for now.</v>

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:09.719
<v Callum Reid>Yeah. Apart from that we're running, but line one's still being a pain with the guarding situation.</v>

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:19.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, on that one, Jamie, can you check the guarding on the line one on Friday? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:27.430
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, alright, Jamie can do that. I'll check the guarding on the line one on Friday.</v>

00:01:28.719 --> 00:01:34.670
<v Callum Reid>Cheers. If we can get that squared away it'll stop the operators moaning at me, so appreciated.</v>

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:39.859
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. And Callum, can you send the shift handover report round?</v>

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.560
<v Callum Reid>Yep, no problem, I'll send the shift handover report round.</v>

00:01:47.969 --> 00:01:49.719
<v Sarah Okafor>Nice one. Fi, planning side?</v>

00:01:52.010 --> 00:02:00.060
<v Fiona Doyle>Um, couple of bits. I finished the repair on the chiller on three last night, so that's done, no action needed there today.</v>

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:02.290
<v Sarah Okafor>Good stuff.</v>

00:02:03.379 --> 00:02:11.080
<v Fiona Doyle>But I still can't get to the number two bearing until production gives us a window, so that's blocked at the minute.</v>

00:02:13.389 --> 00:02:19.340
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, not today I don't think. Maybe later in the week if we get some breathing space.</v>

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:26.449
<v Fiona Doyle>That's fine. Separate one, I'll do the pre-use checks on the trucks by Thursday.</v>

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.159
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fi.</v>

00:02:29.689 --> 00:02:35.639
<v Aisha Begum>Were those the ones parked by dispatch? One of them looked like it'd had a rough night.</v>

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.830
<v Fiona Doyle>Probably has, to be fair.</v>

00:02:40.199 --> 00:02:41.400
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Jamie, stores?</v>

00:02:42.759 --> 00:02:49.060
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah. I've already swapped the filter on the line 1 yesterday, so that's done and out the way.</v>

00:02:50.289 --> 00:02:55.889
<v Jamie Brennan>Still waiting on parts for the Line 3 Chiller, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood, that's just waiting then.</v>

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:06.729
<v Jamie Brennan>And, um, whenever you get a chance, I'll chase the purchase order for the turbine one compressor by end of day.</v>

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.479
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, good, thanks Jamie.</v>

00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:14.199
<v Tomasz Nowak>Worth chasing, that one's been floating about a bit too long.</v>

00:03:15.689 --> 00:03:16.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Tom, maintenance?</v>

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:23.969
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah. I tested the line 2 interlock yesterday and it's all fine now, so that's closed off.</v>

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:25.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Good.</v>

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:35.110
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nothing massive from me otherwise. Just normal checks. And, er, if the rain holds off I might actually get the garden sorted for once.</v>

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.000
<v Callum Reid>It won't.</v>

00:03:39.129 --> 00:03:40.530
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, I know, mate.</v>

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:43.509
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha?</v>

00:03:44.289 --> 00:03:49.539
<v Aisha Begum>Morning. Process side's fairly steady. I've got the water system paperwork still open from yesterday.</v>

00:03:51.879 --> 00:03:57.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Aisha, can you update the risk assessment for work on the water system today?</v>

00:03:58.379 --> 00:04:04.330
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I can do that. I'll update the risk assessment for work on the water system today.</v>

00:04:05.969 --> 00:04:10.520
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. And can you also take vibration readings on the GT1? Low priority.</v>

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:19.740
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, okay. I'll take vibration readings on the GT1. If I don't get to it first thing that's why, but low priority is fine.</v>

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.370
<v Sarah Okafor>That's fine.</v>

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:33.269
<v Grace Liu>On the water system one, just send me the latest version after, Aisha, and I'll have a look. Not a task for stand-up, just so I've seen it.</v>

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:35.949
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, will do.</v>

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.110
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace, anything HSE-wise?</v>

00:04:39.959 --> 00:04:48.009
<v Grace Liu>Nothing major. Just keep the access clear by line one while you're sorting that guarding, because it was getting a bit cluttered yesterday.</v>

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:52.540
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, fair. Half of that wasn't even ours, mind.</v>

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.699
<v Callum Reid>It never is, apparently.</v>

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:02.220
<v Sarah Okafor>Anything else we need to raise, but only if it's actually for today.</v>

00:05:03.509 --> 00:05:08.410
<v Fiona Doyle>No, main thing from me was the blocked bearing job, and that's still blocked.</v>

00:05:08.899 --> 00:05:13.100
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same here, nothing new. The interlock's done, so that's one less headache.</v>

00:05:15.509 --> 00:05:21.459
<v Jamie Brennan>And just to be clear, Line 3 Chiller stays parked till parts land. No point pretending otherwise.</v>

00:05:23.629 --> 00:05:24.829
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep.</v>

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:33.759
<v Callum Reid>For line one, once Jamie's checked the guarding on Friday, we'll know if we can get it fully back to normal.</v>

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:36.879
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah.</v>

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:44.490
<v Sarah Okafor>And Callum, the handover report round this morning please, because yesterday's got a few gaps.</v>

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:50.319
<v Callum Reid>Yep, understood, I'll send the shift handover report round after this.</v>

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.420
<v Aisha Begum>Who's on cake disposal then? Critical path item.</v>

00:05:57.389 --> 00:05:58.589
<v Grace Liu>Low priority.</v>

00:06:00.879 --> 00:06:04.730
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, no, that's holding morale up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Alright, enough. Quick recap then.</v>

00:06:08.699 --> 00:06:15.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie to check the guarding on the line one on Friday, that's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:06:18.019 --> 00:06:20.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Callum to send the shift handover report round.</v>

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:28.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie will chase the purchase order for the turbine one compressor by end of day, whenever you get a chance.</v>

00:06:30.879 --> 00:06:34.730
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha Begum to take vibration readings on the GT1, low priority.</v>

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:39.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha to update the risk assessment for work on the water system today.</v>

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:45.160
<v Sarah Okafor>Fi to do the pre-use checks on the trucks by Thursday.</v>

00:06:45.889 --> 00:06:47.089
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep.</v>

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.500
<v Jamie Brennan>All good.</v>

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:51.410
<v Aisha Begum>Yep.</v>

00:06:52.329 --> 00:06:53.529
<v Callum Reid>Yep, got it.</v>

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:56.680
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sound.</v>

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:58.990
<v Grace Liu>Fine by me.</v>

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:01.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Nice one, thanks all.</v>
